# TD Bank AML Failures — Public Case Analysis

## Executive Summary

This repository contains research and analysis related to the recent TD Bank AML enforcement action.

The purpose of this analysis is to examine:
- AML control failures
- transaction monitoring weaknesses
- suspicious activity escalation issues
- operational risk factors

## Key Observations

- Weak escalation workflows appeared to contribute to risk exposure
- Monitoring systems may have suffered from alert fatigue
- Fragmented investigative processes can reduce effectiveness
- AML staffing and operational culture were recurring themes

## Investigative Relevance

This case demonstrates the importance of:
- strong transaction monitoring systems
- effective SAR escalation procedures
- consistent investigative documentation
- operational coordination across compliance teams

